<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Ph=E1=BA=A7n 10:=
 Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) Deep Dive</h2>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=8C=B1 Ngu=
=E1=BB=93n G=E1=BB=91c &amp; Motivation: Same-Origin Policy Evolution</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Problem Statement</stron=
g>: Browsers implement Same-Origin Policy =C4=91=E1=BB=83 prevent malicious=
 websites from accessing sensitive data from other origins. Nh=C6=B0ng legi=
timate cross-origin requests c=E1=BA=A7n mechanism =C4=91=E1=BB=83 bypass t=
his restriction safely.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Historical Context</stro=
ng>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Early Web (1990s)</stro=
ng>: Simple document sharing, no cross-origin concerns</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>AJAX Era (2005)</strong=
>: XMLHttpRequest enables dynamic content, security concerns arise</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Same-Origin Policy</str=
ong>: Browser security model restricts cross-origin access</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CORS (2014)</strong>: W=
3C standard =C4=91=E1=BB=83 enable controlled cross-origin access</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Modern Web</strong>: AP=
Is, microservices, CDNs require sophisticated cross-origin handling</li>
</ul>
